    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d781">

                <pb facs="0857" n="845" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg845"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/11–1044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-10T19:00:00+03:00">November 10,
                            1944—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4313. ReDept’s 2487, October 20, 10 p.m. On October 25 I wrote to Vyshinski to
                    inform him concerning the public announcement made by the Treasury and War
                    Departments respecting the Allied military mark. I also repeated the request
                    originally made in Ambassador Harriman’s letter of September 11 to Molotov for
                    information on Soviet plans for the use of military currency in Germany. As yet
                    I have had no reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
